From e8c97b15b45adc9212a864abad26066513243d9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RLiOS prot4k <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:47:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] ntdll: Report VirtualQuery regions as runs of identical 4
 KB pages.

get_vprot_range_size() compared whole protection bytes, so (a) the private native bit would split
regions and (b) two uncommitted pages that remember different protections (for example after a
VirtualProtect followed by MEM_DECOMMIT) were reported as two reserved regions, where Windows
reports one. Mask the native bit out and compare uncommitted pages by their committed state only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 6b8942e..e3f6d47 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1190,6 +1190,11 @@ static SIZE_T get_vprot_range_size( char *base, SIZE_T size, BYTE mask, BYTE *vp
 #endif
     *vprot = *vprot_ptr;
 
+    /* The native bit is not visible to Windows, and an uncommitted page has no protection: a run
+     * of uncommitted pages is one region whatever protection bits the pages remember. */
+    mask &= ~VPROT_NATIVE;
+    if ((mask & VPROT_COMMITTED) && !(*vprot & VPROT_COMMITTED)) mask = VPROT_COMMITTED;
+
     /* Page count page table is at least the multiples of sizeof(UINT_PTR)
      * so we don't have to worry about crossing the boundary on unaligned idx values. */
 
